WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:03.818
This is Alika from Toronto, Canada.
我是来自加拿大多伦도의阿利卡。

2
00:00:03.818 --> 00:00:06.142
I was hooked on this show since 2006.
我从2006年起就迷上了这部剧。

3
00:00:06.142 --> 00:00:14.620
In season two when Ted described becoming an architect as inevitable because he had the soul of an artist and the hands of a craftsman.
在第二季中，当特德说成为一名建筑师是命中注定的，因为他既有艺术家的灵魂，又有工匠的双手时，

4
00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:18.758
I began seeing architecture as the perfect balance of art and science.
我开始将建筑学视为艺术与科学的完美平衡。

5
00:00:18.758 --> 00:00:26.620
So when I felt this enchanted with my major, I switched to architecture and today I work as an urban planner at an architecture firm.
所以，当我为自己的专业感到如此着迷时，我转到了建筑专业，如今我在一家建筑事务所担任城市规划师。

6
00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:34.075
I also connected with Ted's creativity, optimism and emotional openness which formed the blueprint for choosing my husband.
我还被特德的创造力、乐观精神和情感上的坦诚所吸引，这成为了我选择丈夫的蓝图。

7
00:00:34.075 --> 00:00:40.620
Being a Canadian I admired Robin's strong personality and Marshall's passion for protecting the environment.
作为一个加拿大人，我很佩服罗宾坚强的性格以及马歇尔对环境保护的热情。

8
00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:45.504
Still till this day, watching old episodes feel like spending time with old friends.
直到今天，看老剧集感觉就像和老朋友叙旧一样。

9
00:00:45.504 --> 00:00:50.620
The show has definitely left a significant imprint on my personal and professional life.
这部剧绝对在我的个人和职业生涯中留下了深刻的印记。

10
00:00:51.620 --> 00:01:00.620
A yellow umbrella, a randomly placed pineapple or a crooked condo floor will always make me smile because how I met your mother is comfort food for the soul.
一把黄雨伞、一个随意放置的菠萝或一处歪斜的公寓楼层总能让我会心一笑，因为《老爸老妈浪漫史》就像是滋养心灵的慰藉美食。

11
00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:06.839
I'm alone, won't be super city.
我独自一人，不会去太大的城市。

12
00:01:06.839 --> 00:01:20.080
When I see he's permit me to tell you everything in New York City.
当我看到他允许我在纽约市告诉你一切时。

13
00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:23.536
Well hello folks, welcome to another episode of How We Made Your Mother.
各位好，欢迎收看另一期的《我们是如何创作老爸老妈浪漫史的》。

14
00:01:23.536 --> 00:01:24.304
I'm Josh Radner.
我是乔什·拉德纳。

15
00:01:24.304 --> 00:01:26.080
I'm here with my friend Craig Thomas.
我和我的朋友克雷格·托马斯在这里。

16
00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:26.638
Hey Josh.
嘿，乔什。

17
00:01:26.638 --> 00:01:31.098
Years ago Craig and I made a show together called How I Met Your Mother.
多年前，我和克雷格一起制作了一部名为《老爸老妈浪漫史》的剧。

18
00:01:31.098 --> 00:01:33.080
I played Ted Mosby on that show.
我在剧中扮演特德·莫斯比。

19
00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:36.053
Craig co-created the show with Carter Bayes.
克雷格与卡特·贝斯共同创作了这部剧。

20
00:01:36.053 --> 00:01:39.296
We're talking about the show and we're now deep.
我们在谈论这部剧，而且现在已经深入探讨了。

21
00:01:39.296 --> 00:01:40.107
Are we deep?
我们算深入探讨了吗？

22
00:01:40.107 --> 00:01:43.080
We're still at the beginning of season four.
我们目前还在第四季的初期。

23
00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:45.796
We're talking today about episode three.
我们今天要聊的是第四季第三集。

24
00:01:45.796 --> 00:01:54.080
I love New Jersey but before we get to that I will say I hear from so many people who say I'm an architect because of you.
我热爱新泽西，但在我们聊到这个之前，我要说我听到很多人说：‘因为你，我才成为了一名建筑师。’

25
00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:56.533
That is insane, right?
这太疯狂了，对吧？

26
00:01:56.533 --> 00:01:59.835
And no spoilers, you are not in fact an architect.
剧透一下，你事实上并不是建筑师。

27
00:01:59.835 --> 00:02:01.222
I'm not an architect.
我不是建筑师。

28
00:02:01.222 --> 00:02:02.080
That's weird.
这真奇怪。

29
00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:14.080
And I probably architecturally I related the most to episode two season one when he showed Robin his cool architecture tools and held them up.
而且在建筑方面，我可能最感同身受的是第一季第二集，当时他向罗宾展示他那些酷炫的建筑工具并把它们举起来。

30
00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:15.970
That's what I know about architecture.
这就是我对建筑学的全部了解了。

31
00:02:15.970 --> 00:02:18.257
That was the full extent of your architecture.
那确实是你对建筑学了解的全部范围。

32
00:02:18.257 --> 00:02:23.080
I told you that a grad school asked me to be their commencement speaker in Oklahoma or somewhere.
我告诉过你，俄克拉荷马州还是哪里的某所研究生院邀请我去作毕业典礼演讲。

33
00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:27.468
I ended up doing it for some reason but I always thought that was so funny.
不知为什么我最后还真去了，但我一直觉得这太搞笑了。

34
00:02:27.468 --> 00:02:31.681
They said that you're the most famous TV architect previous generations.
他们说你是前几代人中最著名的电视建筑师。

35
00:02:31.681 --> 00:02:34.080
It was Mike Brady and now it's Ted Mosby.
以前是迈克·布雷迪，现在是特德·莫斯比。

36
00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:36.990
Oh, that's a great honor that he was the TV architect.
哦，能成为电视建筑师真是个巨大的荣誉。

37
00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:38.823
He was the coach at the architect.
他是建筑师里的教练。

38
00:02:38.823 --> 00:02:40.278
Oh my God, that's an honor.
天哪，这真是一种荣誉。

39
00:02:40.278 --> 00:02:41.733
Ted has replaced Mr. Brady.
特德已经取代了布雷迪先生。

40
00:02:41.733 --> 00:02:43.080
Take the head, Mr. Brady.
接替吧，布雷迪先生。

41
00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:46.064
And I like that combination of art and science.
我喜欢艺术与科学的结合。

42
00:02:46.064 --> 00:02:51.080
The hands of a craftsman but the soul of an artiSt. I think that's really cool.
工匠的双手，艺术家的灵魂。我觉得这真的很酷。

43
00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:52.673
Thanks for that great letter.
谢谢这封精彩的来信。

44
00:02:52.673 --> 00:02:56.080
We love hearing from people about what the show meant to them.
我们很乐意听大家讲述这部剧对他们的意义。

45
00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:59.637
And let's charge onward in our in our journey through season four.
让我们继续踏上第四季的旅程吧。

46
00:02:59.637 --> 00:03:03.409
This episode that we're talking about is episode three of season four.
我们今天要聊的这一集是第四季第三集。

47
00:03:03.409 --> 00:03:05.080
It's called I Heart New Jersey.
它叫《我爱新泽西》。

48
00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:06.655
Is that how you say it?
是这么念的吗？

49
00:03:06.655 --> 00:03:08.436
It's not Heart New Jersey.
不是‘心系新泽西’。

50
00:03:08.436 --> 00:03:12.683
I Heart New Jersey, written by I believe Greg Maylands, a.k.a.
是《我爱新泽西》，编剧我相信是格雷格·梅兰兹，也就是

51
00:03:12.683 --> 00:03:15.080
Greg Mulan's as I like to call him.
我喜欢管他叫格雷格·穆兰（Greg Mulan）。

52
00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:17.144
I think that's his preferred pronunciation.
我想那是他比较喜欢的发音。

53
00:03:17.144 --> 00:03:18.872
I'm just proud to get the right way.
我只是为自己发音正确而感到骄傲。

54
00:03:18.872 --> 00:03:21.080
That's the Ted way that he would pronounce it.
这就是他会念的“泰德式”发音。

55
00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:29.080
The great Greg Maylands only writer to write for both friends and how I met your mother I think is the fun fact about Greg and he did a great earlier.
伟大的格雷格·梅兰兹（Greg Maylands），他是唯一一位同时为《老友记》和《老爸老妈浪漫史》写过剧本的编剧，我想这是关于格雷格的一个趣事，他之前表现得很棒。

56
00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:36.080
One of his early episodes he came on and talked about it to go back and listen to that is the great Greg Maylands and this is really great one that he wrote in season four.
他早期的一集里曾来聊过这个，大家可以回头去听听，这就是伟大的格雷格·梅兰兹，而这一集是他第四季里写得非常棒的一集。

57
00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:38.453
Yeah, this is this is Alec.
对，这是……这是亚历克（Alec）。

58
00:03:38.453 --> 00:03:39.572
When did this one air?
这一集是什么时候播出的？

59
00:03:39.572 --> 00:03:42.165
Alec Alec we have to we should warn you is his air.
亚历克……我们得提醒你一下，这是他的空气声。

60
00:03:42.165 --> 00:03:43.080
Can you hear that?
你听到了吗？

61
00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:43.690
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

62
00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:44.843
That's Alex Eric.
那是亚历克的风声。

63
00:03:44.843 --> 00:03:48.165
Alec is in some sort of a wind tunnel experiment.
亚历克正身处某种风洞实验中。

64
00:03:48.165 --> 00:03:51.080
There's an air dynamic to a vacuum cleaner.
吸尘器也有空气动力学原理。

65
00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:52.256
It's a carbine.
这是个卡宾枪。

66
00:03:52.256 --> 00:03:55.080
I have a data farm here in my house.
我家里有个数据农场。

67
00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:57.628
I think how loud we can get it.
我在想要把声音开多大才行。

68
00:03:57.628 --> 00:04:01.080
This episode aired on October 6th of 2028.
这一集是在2028年10月6日播出的。

69
00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:02.369
Okay.
好的。

70
00:04:02.369 --> 00:04:02.948
Thank you.
谢谢。

71
00:04:02.948 --> 00:04:07.460
So Greg, give us a little armchair summary of what what this episode is about.
那么，格雷格，给我们简单概括一下这一集讲的是什么吧。

72
00:04:07.460 --> 00:04:09.080
I thought it was a good one.
我觉得这一集挺不错的。

73
00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:09.880
It's a good one.
这是一集好剧。

74
00:04:09.880 --> 00:04:10.680
It's a good one.
确实不错。

75
00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:12.580
And it's in mostly off campus episode.
而且这主要是一集发生在校园之外的剧。

76
00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:14.030
I think about these episodes.
我对这类剧集的看法是这样的。

77
00:04:14.030 --> 00:04:18.080
These are hard to make good where the gang is mostly not in their place of power.
这些剧很难拍好，因为主角们大多不在他们势力范围内。

78
00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:24.080
They're mostly not in like the fortress of solitude or like the sort of energy center of all of justice, whatever.
他们基本上不在那座孤独堡垒里，也不在正义能量中心之类的地方。

79
00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:28.966
This is an off campus episode because they go to New Jersey because Ted is getting very, very serious.
这是一集校外剧，因为他们去了新泽西，因为泰德开始变得非常非常认真。

80
00:04:28.966 --> 00:04:32.080
He's engaged to Stella who lives in New Jersey with her daughter.
他和住在新泽西、带着女儿的斯特拉（Stella）订婚了。

81
00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:44.080
And he is so tired of the commute back and forth to always see her that he convinces his friends while Stella invites them all to come hang out in New Jersey to prove how great New Jersey is in that Ted will be happy there.
他厌倦了为了见她而两头跑的通勤生活，于是他说服了朋友们——而斯特拉也邀请他们一起来新泽西玩，好证明新泽西有多棒，并且泰德在那里也会很开心。

82
00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:50.080
Ted is under the impression they are going to marry and move to New York and Stella is the impression that the opposite is happening.
泰德以为他们会结婚并搬到纽约，而斯特拉则以为情况正好相反。

83
00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:51.495
He's coming to New Jersey.
是他要搬到新泽西去。

84
00:04:51.495 --> 00:04:52.856
They don't know this yet.
他们现在还不知道这一点。

85
00:04:52.856 --> 00:04:58.080
It's yet again on that theme of not really knowing each other, maybe well enough to get married.
这再次契合了那个主题，即彼此了解得其实还不够深，或许还没到足以结婚的地步。

86
00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:01.893
And it kind of all blows up from there, which place are we going to live?
事情随后全面爆发了，他们到底要在哪里生活？

87
00:05:01.893 --> 00:05:05.080
And a lot of worms come out of a lot of cans because of that.
因为这个，各种麻烦和问题全都涌现出来了。

88
00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:10.832
I thought, you know, on the surface, this is an episode with a lot of New Jersey jokes.
我觉得，表面上看，这一集有很多关于新泽西的笑话。

89
00:05:10.832 --> 00:05:13.080
You know, apologies to New Jersey.
向新泽西道个歉。

90
00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:15.774
And a lot of great local news jokes.
还有很多很棒的当地新闻笑话。

91
00:05:15.774 --> 00:05:24.080
You know, there's a lot of like just fun bits in this episode, but it's also about something bigger and larger.
你知道的，这一集里有很多有趣的桥段，但它同时也探讨了更深远、更大的主题。

92
00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:25.754
Jordana quotes this thing.
乔达娜（Jordana）引用过这样一句话。

93
00:05:25.754 --> 00:05:27.556
It might be a sterile thing.
这可能是斯特拉说过的话。

94
00:05:27.556 --> 00:05:32.835
I can't remember, but Jordana has said to me, and I didn't originate with Jordana.
我记不太清了，但乔达娜跟我说过，而且这话不是乔达娜原创的。

95
00:05:32.835 --> 00:05:39.080
That's all I'm saying, that you can have a lot of love stories, but not everyone is a life story.
我想说的是，你可以有很多段爱情故事，但并非每一段都能成为人生故事。

96
00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:47.918
And for me, I think part of what Ted is coming to realize here or what he's navigating is that you can love someone.
对我而言，我觉得泰德在这里逐渐意识到、或者说他正在应对的事情之一，就是你可以爱一个人。

97
00:05:47.918 --> 00:05:50.080
You can be attracted to someone.
你可以被某人吸引。

98
00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:55.354
The chemistry can be off the charts, the repartake can be off the charts, all of that stuff.
你们之间可能会有极佳的化学反应，妙语连珠的互动也可能火花四溅，诸如此类。

99
00:05:55.354 --> 00:05:59.080
But so much else has to line up for the life story to take place.
但除此之外，还有太多其他的事情必须契合，人生故事才能真正上演。

100
00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:06.080
It's insane how many things need to link up and how it's crazy that it ever happens.
有那么多事情需要完美对接，这简直太疯狂了，而且能成真本身就是一个奇迹。

101
00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:07.080
Totally.
完全同意。

102
00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:09.757
It's like the divorce rate is 50% or whatever.
离婚率就像是有 50% 还是什么的。

103
00:06:09.757 --> 00:06:10.514
That's crazy.
太疯狂了。

104
00:06:10.514 --> 00:06:12.202
It's a miracle it ever works.
能维持下去简直是个奇迹。

105
00:06:12.202 --> 00:06:12.842
It's crazy.
太疯狂了。

106
00:06:12.842 --> 00:06:18.080
We should look at it as a huge success rate that 50% of the time enough boxes are checked.
我们应该换个角度来看，只要有 50% 的概率满足了各项条件，这就已经是相当高的成功率了。

107
00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:22.080
I think we need to look at the glass half full kind of, but in sort of a negative way.
我觉得我们得用乐观的心态来看待半满的水杯，不过是以一种相对消极的方式。

108
00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:29.080
I think that this is why another reason people respond to the show is because it's a weird, because it's a show about growing up.
我觉得这也是人们对这部剧有共鸣的另一个原因，因为它很古怪，因为它是一部关于成长的剧。

109
00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:33.595
A lot of growing up is, you know, there's dashed hopes.
成长的很大一部分，你知道的，就是希望破灭。

110
00:06:33.595 --> 00:06:36.468
You renegotiate with your idealism.
你与自己的理想主义重新谈判。

111
00:06:36.468 --> 00:06:40.080
We see that a lot with Marshall and his job.
我们在马歇尔和他的工作上经常看到这一点。

112
00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:48.080
And I think that Ted's big negotiation is around just because you spotted someone across the room and you connected.
而且我认为泰德面临的重大妥协是，不能仅仅因为你隔着房间看到了某个人并产生了连接。

113
00:06:49.080 --> 00:06:54.080
He's got very youthful, almost like cinematic ideas about love and how it should be and how it should feel.
他有着非常年轻、甚至有点像电影情节一样的爱情观念，关于它应该是什么样，应该有什么感觉。

114
00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:56.580
And he keeps tripping up against these details.
而他却不断在这些细节上栽跟头。

115
00:06:56.580 --> 00:06:59.080
He falls in love with a woman who doesn't want.
他爱上了一个不想要的女人。

116
00:06:59.080 --> 00:06:59.727
Yeah, yeah.
对，对。

117
00:06:59.727 --> 00:07:03.551
He falls in love with a woman who, he loves everything about her.
他爱上了一个女人，他爱她身上的方方面面。

118
00:07:03.551 --> 00:07:05.080
She doesn't want children.
她不想要孩子。

119
00:07:05.080 --> 00:07:06.593
He desperately wants children.
而他极其渴望孩子。

120
00:07:06.593 --> 00:07:11.080
He falls in love with a woman who she'll stay in the tri-state area, but it's New Jersey.
他爱上了一个女人，她虽然愿意留在三州地区，但那是新泽西。

121
00:07:11.080 --> 00:07:12.735
And he's like, no, no, no.
而他的反应是，不，不，不。

122
00:07:12.735 --> 00:07:16.425
Ted Mosby lives in New York in the mythology of Ted Mosby.
在泰德·莫斯比的观念里，泰德·莫斯比是住在纽约的。

123
00:07:16.425 --> 00:07:18.080
He lives in New York City.
他住在纽约市。

124
00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:18.446
Yeah.
对。

125
00:07:18.446 --> 00:07:21.885
So he's constantly tripping up against reality.
所以他不断地在现实面前碰壁。

126
00:07:21.885 --> 00:07:24.080
And it's fascinating to watch.
看着这个过程非常吸引人。

127
00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:24.487
It is.
确实如此。

128
